Size the activity bar overflow from the room its siblings leave.

Written when the mobile stylesheet hid the Manage section, which freed vertical
space that this.dimension was measured before. The overflow calculation then
moved icons into the "..." menu while the room for them was visibly there -- on
a phone that was every view: Explorer, Search, Source Control, Run and Debug and
Extensions all ended up behind the menu. The hide was removed on 2026-08-15,
and the fix holds either way: it reads the room the siblings actually leave,
whatever is or is not shown around the bar.

Reading the bar's own clientHeight does not fix it and makes it worse. That
height is the RESULT of how many icons fit, so once they overflow the element
collapses to one row and reports 48px, and the calculation can never recover.
Measured on a 863px bar: the element read 48 while 732 were free, room for 15
icons rather than 1.

What is actually available is what the siblings leave in the parent -- the
compact menubar above and the global actions below. Read through
document.querySelector rather than a field because this class is handed its
container by a caller that does not retain it, scoped to .activitybar so the
panel's own composite bar is untouched, and falling back to the cached value
when the query does not match or measures zero.

